, $15.1M on hand vs. Collins' $1.1M)", "Expert ratings consensus of Likely D or better from all 11 raters", "Prediction markets price Ossoff at 97% to win"], "rationale": "Every recent poll shows Ossoff leading by 8-15 points, including surveys from Republican-leaning pollsters, and he holds an overwhelming cash advantage over Collins. Markets and expert ratings align on a comfortable incumbent win, so a Safe D rating with a mid-single-digit-to-high-single-digit expected margin fits the evidence.", "watch": "A late turnout differential or consolidated Republican coattails from the governor's race could narrow the margin more than polls anticipate.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Ossoff (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Jon Ossoff seeks a second term against Representative Mike Collins in a state that leans slightly Republican but has favored Democrats in recent statewide contests. Polling throughout the fall has been remarkably consistent, with Ossoff leading by roughly 8 to 15 points in surveys from both Republican-affiliated and independent pollsters, including an Atlanta Journal-Constitution poll in late October. Averages place the race around 8 to 9 points in Ossoff's favor.\n\nThe resource picture is lopsided: Ossoff has raised over $115 million and holds about $15 million on hand, while Collins has roughly $1.1 million available. Outside spending has been minimal on both sides. All eleven expert ratings put the race at Likely D or stronger, and prediction markets price Ossoff's chances at about 97 percent. The main remaining question is turnout, not the margin's direction.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9499, "margin": 8.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9449, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9229, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9348, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9317, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9355, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-2